/*
 * The SPU instruction set (IBM SPU ISA v1.2 as implemented by the Cell BE), as an X-macro:
 *
 *   PS_SPU_OP(id, mnemonic, format, opbits, opcode, flags)
 *
 * id        Op enumerator (pspocket/spu/decoder.hpp)
 * mnemonic  assembler mnemonic
 * format    operand format (Fmt), drives decoding, disassembly, register usage and the generic encoder
 * opbits    width of the opcode field at the top of the word: 11 (RR), 10 (RI8), 9 (RI16), 8 (RI10), 7 (RI18,
 *           hint-relative/absolute), 4 (RRR)
 * opcode    opcode value in those bits
 * flags     OPF_* (decoder.hpp)
 *
 * Opcode values follow RPCS3's decoder table, rpcs3/Emu/Cell/SPUOpcodes.h (spu_decoder). dfceq/dfcmeq/dfcgt/dfcmgt
 * and dftsv exist in SPU ISA 1.2 but not on the PS3's Cell BE: they decode, disassemble and raise an illegal
 * instruction (as RPCS3, which treats them as UNK).
 */

